Crash that disabled the top bar (do not reintroduce)

On login after this restyle, macos-top-panel@local.dev went to State: ERROR (still listed in enabled-extensions, but not running). Journal:

TypeError: Object is of type St.Widget - cannot convert to StScrollable
AppLauncherOverlay@.../lib/appLauncher.js  (set_child)
enable@.../extension.js

GNOME 50 St.ScrollView.set_child() requires an St.Scrollable. St.BoxLayout is one. A bare St.Widget with Clutter.GridLayout is not. Putting the grid directly in the scroll view aborted enable() and took the entire top panel with it.

Correct:

this._gridHost = new St.BoxLayout({orientation: Clutter.Orientation.VERTICAL, x_expand: true});
this._grid = new St.Widget({layout_manager: new Clutter.GridLayout(), width: COLUMNS * CELL_WIDTH});
this._gridHost.add_child(this._grid);
this._scroll.set_child(this._gridHost);  // BoxLayout, never the grid widget

Same pattern as Wi-Fi/Bluetooth lists (set_child(this._networksBox) on a St.BoxLayout).

enable() also wraps new AppLauncherOverlay() in try/catch and logErrors so a future launcher bug cannot disable the rest of the panel. disable() already does this._appLauncher?.destroy().

If it happens again: gnome-extensions info macos-top-panel@local.dev → State: ERROR. Then journalctl --user -b -g 'macos-top-panel' for the TypeError. Fix disk + live overlay, then the user can enable it (no extra logout required for a failed-to-load extension — enable loads current files).





5. Mirror / extend to a TV (not Apple AirPlay)

Linux cannot AirPlay to a Roku. Roku AirPlay is Apple-only. peachOS uses Miracast / Wi-Fi Display (Roku “Screen mirroring”).

Packages / launchers (this laptop)





gnome-network-displays 0.99.0-1 — /usr/bin/gnome-network-displays



Encoder: gstreamer1.0-fdkaac (fdkaacenc, rank primary). Do not rely on avenc_aac (rank none); TVs often get picture and no sound



Also present: x264enc, openh264enc



User launcher: ~/.local/share/applications/peachos-connect-tv.desktop
Name: Connect to TV
Exec: env NETWORK_DISPLAYS_AAC_ENC=fdkaacenc NETWORK_DISPLAYS_H264_ENC=x264enc gnome-network-displays



Transient run: systemctl --user start peachos-network-displays.service if it was started with systemd-run --user --unit=peachos-network-displays

Wi-Fi chip (Intel AX211) already exposes p2p-dev-wlp0s20f3. UFW is ENABLED=no in /etc/ufw/ufw.conf.

TV side

Roku: Settings → System → Screen mirroring → Prompt or Always allow.

In the app: pick the TV. This screen = mirror. Virtual screen (0.91+) = closest thing to extend (compressed extra desktop, not a real DRM connector). HDMI is still the only low-latency true extend.

Audio: why speakers stayed on, and the router

GND creates a PipeWire null sink named like gnome_network_displays_gnome-ne (“GNOME Network Displays”) and captures its monitor for AAC. Apps still play to the default sink (laptop speakers) unless that default is switched.

Live helper:





Script: ~/.local/share/peachos/tv-audio/peachos-tv-audio



Unit: ~/.config/systemd/user/peachos-tv-audio.service (WantedBy=graphical-session.target)

Behavior:





pactl subscribe until a sink matching gnome_network_displays appears



Save previous default sink



pactl set-default-sink to the TV sink and move-sink-input all current streams



When the TV sink vanishes (cast ended), restore the previous sink and move streams back

This does not invent a second audio protocol. If the Roku never negotiates WFD AAC 48 kHz stereo (modes & 0x1 in gnome-network-displays wfd-client.c), GND sends video only. fdkaac makes AAC that actually muxes; it cannot add LPCM (GND does not implement LPCM). If a recast with fdkaac is still silent, inspect journalctl --user -u peachos-network-displays / G_MESSAGES_DEBUG=all for WfdAudioCodec: and An audiocodec has been selected.

Debug env: NETWORK_DISPLAYS_AAC_ENC=fdkaacenc, NETWORK_DISPLAYS_H264_ENC=x264enc, G_MESSAGES_DEBUG=all.

There is a separate app Mirror (app.mirror.Mirror.desktop) — that is an AirPlay receiver (phone → this laptop), the opposite direction. Do not confuse it with Connect to TV.





